SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil: Freedom on the Net 2022 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2022","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/brazil/freedom-net/2022","claim":"Freedom House said Bolsonaro and his allies were a key source of election disinformation, that Bolsonaro made at least 6,000 false or misleading statements by August 2022, and that these claims were reproduced through official channels and social media as a well-financed disinformation machine.","locator":"country report narrative under election disinformation discussion","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reputable independent rights monitor synthesizing contemporaneous evidence and fact-checking counts; not a court finding, but strong secondary documentation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly about 2022 campaign behavior.","ruler_attribution":"Directly about Bolsonaro and his allies; the report ties the statements to his office, campaign, and official communication channels.","contrary_evidence":["The report is secondary synthesis, not a judicial finding.","It captures a pattern, not each individual false claim."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro supera 6.000 declarações falsas ou distorcidas no início da campanha pela reeleição","publisher":"Aos Fatos","publication_date":"2022-08-17","url":"https://www.aosfatos.org/noticias/bolsonaro-supera-6000-declaracoes-falsas-ou-distorcidas-no-inicio-da-campanha-pela-reeleicao/","claim":"Aos Fatos counted at least 6,042 false or distorted claims by Bolsonaro since the start of his presidency and noted that his repeated falsehoods included claims that his government had no corruption scandals.","locator":"opening summary and first analytic paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Specialized fact-checking outlet with transparent counting method and direct examples; not an official record but highly relevant on truthfulness.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific; the claims are his own public statements while in office and as a candidate.","contrary_evidence":["Fact-check counts do not measure intent for every statement.","The article is a fact-check summary, not a court judgment."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro mentiu mais de quatro vezes por dia durante governo","publisher":"Aos Fatos","publication_date":"2022-12-29","url":"https://www.aosfatos.org/noticias/mentiras-bolsonaro/","claim":"Aos Fatos concluded Bolsonaro ended his presidency with 6,676 false or distorted statements, including repeated false claims about corruption, the pandemic, the economy, and the Pix payment system.","locator":"sections 'Negacionismo prevalece', 'Mentiras repetidas', and 'Longe do real'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Longitudinal fact-check compilation with explicit counts and recurring themes; strong for pattern evidence, weaker for legal culpability.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Covers 2022 and the end of Bolsonaro's term.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific and attributable to his public record as president and candidate.","contrary_evidence":["A fact-check ledger cannot prove motive in every instance.","It is a cumulative press compilation rather than an adjudicated finding."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Moraes condena coligação Pelo Bem do Brasil por litigância de má-fé e aplica multa de R$ 22,9 milhões","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022-11-23","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Novembro/moraes-condena-coligacao-pelo-bem-do-brasil-por-litigancia-de-ma-fe-e-aplica-multa-de-r-22-9-milhoes","claim":"The TSE president said the coalition backing Bolsonaro's runoff challenge relied on 'absolutely false' arguments and fined the coalition R$22.9 million for bad-faith litigation over a supposed second-round urn verification.","locator":"headline and opening paragraphs","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official electoral-court order with explicit legal finding and sanction.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target year, after the runoff.","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Bolsonaro's coalition and campaign litigation, though the formal party actor was the coalition rather than Bolsonaro alone.","contrary_evidence":["The decision targets coalition litigation, not a personal criminal finding against Bolsonaro.","It concerns post-election conduct rather than routine governing."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7","7B.8"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"TSE mantém na Justiça Eleitoral julgamento de ação de investigação contra Jair Bolsonaro e Braga Netto","publisher":"Tribunal Superior Eleitoral","publication_date":"2022-12-13","url":"https://www.tse.jus.br/comunicacao/noticias/2022/Dezembro/tse-mantem-na-justica-eleitoral-julgamento-de-acao-de-investigacao-contra-jair-bolsonaro-e-braga-netto","claim":"The TSE unanimously rejected objections and kept in electoral court the investigation into Bolsonaro and Braga Netto over the July 2022 ambassadors meeting that attacked the voting system with false claims.","locator":"headline and first paragraph","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official court decision directly addressing Bolsonaro's conduct and the legal basis for scrutiny.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022 and about a 2022 act.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific: the meeting was hosted by him as president and candidate, with Braga Netto as his ticket mate.","contrary_evidence":["This is an investigation-maintenance ruling, not a final merits judgment.","It shows ongoing scrutiny rather than final liability."],"lenses":["7B.6","7B.7"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil's Bolsonaro hints at potential replacement of Petrobras CEO","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-03-16","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/stock-market-news/brazils-bolsonaro-hints-at-potential-replacement-of-petrobras-ceo-2786154","claim":"Bolsonaro publicly said replacing Petrobras' chief executive was possible after fuel-price criticism and indicated that anyone in government could be replaced if not doing the job satisfactorily.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting on Bolsonaro's own statements and their policy context; strong contemporaneous evidence of politicized pressure.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro's own public pressure on a state company, though the corporate board ultimately remained a separate institutional actor.","contrary_evidence":["The statement alone does not prove unlawful self-dealing.","Some intervention was framed as fuel-price policy rather than personal gain."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Petrobras shares drop following CEO ouster, fuel price woes","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/commodities-news/petrobras-shares-drop-following-ceo-ouster-fuel-price-woes-2829730","claim":"Reuters reported that Bolsonaro's government ousted Petrobras's chief executive for the second time in two months and signaled plans to alter the company's market-based fuel pricing policy after Bolsonaro railed against price increases.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters coverage of a concrete personnel action and policy pressure on a state-controlled company.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Bolsonaro as president, because the article describes his political pressure and the ensuing executive ouster.","contrary_evidence":["The move is easier to read as politicized pressure than personal enrichment.","It concerns corporate control rather than private gain."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Bolsonaro indica que vai trocar diretoria da Petrobras","publisher":"UOL / Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-26","url":"https://noticias.uol.com.br/ultimas-noticias/reuters/2022/05/26/bolsonaro-indica-que-vai-trocar-diretoria-da-petrobras.htm","claim":"Bolsonaro said he had the right to propose changes to Petrobras's board and management and indicated the changes would come soon, framing the company as something he could reshape through the government.","locator":"lead paragraphs and Bolsonaro quote section","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters syndicated report of Bolsonaro's explicit statement about replacing state-company leadership.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly Bolsonaro-specific, because it quotes his own public claim of authority over Petrobras management.","contrary_evidence":["Corporate governance is partly institutional, so the statement is not itself proof of illegality.","The quote reflects intent and pressure, not the final outcome."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.9"]}

SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Brazil government to veto 3.1 billion reais in budget items to fund payroll -sources","publisher":"Reuters","publication_date":"2022-01-21","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economic-indicators/brazil-government-to-veto-31-billion-reais-in-budget-items-to-fund-payroll-sources-2745305","claim":"Reuters reported that Bolsonaro's government planned to veto R$3.1 billion in discretionary spending, while keeping the electoral fund at R$4.9 billion, because a larger cut would be politically difficult in an election year.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on an election-year budget choice with clear political tradeoffs.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributable to Bolsonaro's government and election-year incentives, though the budget process also involved Congress and ministries.","contrary_evidence":["This is a political-budget tradeoff, not direct personal enrichment.","The article relies on unnamed sources rather than a signed government statement."],"lenses":["7B.8","7B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
I considered roughly 30 documents across official court releases, Reuters/UOL syndicated reporting, fact-checking compilations, and rights-monitor reports. I retained items that showed Bolsonaro's own statements, his coalition's legal conduct, or his administration's direct use of state power for political advantage. I rejected or downgraded broad Brazil corruption indicators, generic democracy scores, and open-ended allegations that lacked a ruler-specific personal nexus. I also avoided older or out-of-period material when it was only useful as background rather than 2022 evidence. Repeated Reuters syndications of the same Petrobras or IPEA stories were treated as duplicates unless they added a materially distinct claim.

**Remaining gaps**
The weakest area is direct personal or family enrichment in 2022. I found stronger evidence for deliberate falsehoods, bad-faith litigation, and politicized use of state companies than for private monetary gain, hidden assets, or family profiteering. More search would help on asset declarations, campaign-finance scrutiny, gifts, procurement, and any 2022 audit or court finding tying Bolsonaro or close relatives to self-dealing. Evidence on whether he corrected false claims after notice is also thinner than evidence that he doubled down.
